#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096417 :question/id #uuid "d7a77a89-0535-54da-a246-36ee5b4e9e7f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3634" :question/problem "Differentiate $x\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\cos x .$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t (x\\cos x)' &=   u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t&= (x)'\\cdot \\cos x + x\\cdot (\\cos x)'\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t   & = 1 \\cdot \\cos x + x (-\\sin x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t  & =  \\cos x - x \\sin x\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096418 :question/id #uuid "6bb0eded-7277-5ab5-8c13-bfc480403b1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3635" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=x^2\\ln x,$ find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}ln⁡x+{x}^{2}{(ln⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot ln⁡x+{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\  & =2xln⁡x+x \\\\  & =x(2ln⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096419 :question/id #uuid "072ce609-b04d-57b0-9c7d-cbb8765c38fa" :question/math-academy-id "e-3636" :question/problem "If a curve $\\mathcal C$ is given by $y=e^x\\sin x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\dfrac \\pi 2.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x) = e^x$ and $v(x)=\\sin{x}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = e^x,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos x.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot cos⁡x+sin⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(cos⁡x+sin⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\dfrac\\pi 2$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi /2} & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(cos⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+sin⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(0+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi /2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $e^{\\pi/2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca48a7b-5c44-5ceb-9f7a-46475643a906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}x-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094898} {:answer/id #uuid "bb75f041-eacc-5451-b3bf-166b8949e018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}x-2x\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094899} {:answer/id #uuid "be19c12b-7932-58a0-8911-03fae070336e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}x-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094900} {:answer/id #uuid "01d55ed0-9518-50b6-bd31-eee6e6062db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}x-2x\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094901} {:answer/id #uuid "7c36000d-a170-5e76-a4c2-7f56fa11b4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be19c12b-7932-58a0-8911-03fae070336e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}x-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094900} :answer-field/id #uuid "176e6625-97a1-5955-aa6f-db131e85d138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094897}] :question/id #uuid "637cc150-7613-534a-bd8b-a83dc2342647" :question/math-academy-id "q-1907" :question/problem "Differentiate $x^{2}\\cos x$." :question/worked-solution "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)=- x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0160d55-41e0-5207-b70c-5dfc23c09ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\log_{3} x}{x} + \\frac{5\\ln x}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094946} {:answer/id #uuid "c7990de4-7764-55e3-9375-eb40c109bc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}x}{x\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094947} {:answer/id #uuid "d09b4047-e57a-53fc-a06a-395be25f2765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\log_{3} x}{x} + \\frac{\\ln x}{x\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094948} {:answer/id #uuid "335f8a22-7cb0-58d7-b32a-65b960fb6f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\log_{3} x}{x} + \\frac{5\\ln x}{x\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094949} {:answer/id #uuid "667ba516-4fd4-5570-a622-0203f2df6f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\log_{3} x}{x} + \\frac{5}{x\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "335f8a22-7cb0-58d7-b32a-65b960fb6f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\log_{3} x}{x} + \\frac{5\\ln x}{x\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094949} :answer-field/id #uuid "39bd020b-c912-5ba2-9e81-38edfaf9381b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094945}] :question/id #uuid "cf22f993-a76b-52d8-8977-b83456911b64" :question/math-academy-id "q-1933" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = 5\\log_{3} x\\ln x$, find $f^{′}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5 \\log{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}}{\\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\right)=\\frac{10 \\log{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9123bd43-0985-5815-be98-b4a9d900c88c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095389} {:answer/id #uuid "c878d6c7-8a8f-5afe-acd0-f6083b75b15d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}x(2x+\\operatorname{sec}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095390} {:answer/id #uuid "cafc2f88-c0bc-5677-aebd-e70ab8b877b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095391} {:answer/id #uuid "098c202e-114f-59ad-a524-c2dbaf56709e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2\\tan x + x\\sec^{2} x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095392} {:answer/id #uuid "72022765-1175-5b0d-bf32-d2786a419e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}x(2+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{tan}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "098c202e-114f-59ad-a524-c2dbaf56709e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2\\tan x + x\\sec^{2} x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095392} :answer-field/id #uuid "634e8d5c-10ef-5420-b752-d09396e5a6f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095388}] :question/id #uuid "af8066b5-6cf6-5662-aded-c14a5c3d72ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-47965" :question/problem "Differentiate $x^{2}\\tan x$." :question/worked-solution "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(x^{2} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)=x^{2} \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right) + 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bee14b33-9a9a-566f-ae0f-b70db7b75c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x^{-4}\\log_{2} x + x^{-3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095395} {:answer/id #uuid "65a54537-8926-5d90-9de3-43e22ca3f920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{x}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095396} {:answer/id #uuid "6d25aa7d-6713-5cdb-87e2-d99151b0b223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{-3}(3\\log_{2} x - \\frac{1}{\\ln 2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095397} {:answer/id #uuid "73dfd687-de90-55f0-b921-6721f070fe6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{x}^{-4}+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095398} {:answer/id #uuid "755d2bb5-e695-529e-993a-f34c357b92bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{-4}(-3\\log_{2} x + \\frac{1}{\\ln 2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "755d2bb5-e695-529e-993a-f34c357b92bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{-4}(-3\\log_{2} x + \\frac{1}{\\ln 2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095399} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a360a42-15ec-5c13-a47a-98daac46dc09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095394}] :question/id #uuid "baeb19e8-14cf-5247-8232-e1d3e9bfdf54" :question/math-academy-id "q-47966" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = x^{-3}\\log_{2} x$, find $f^{′}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{\\log{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{3} \\log{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)=- \\frac{3 \\log{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{4} \\log{\\left(2 \\right)}} + \\frac{1}{x^{4} \\log{\\left(2 \\right)}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a701631f-ee6f-5c74-8945-ae030b322172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095407} {:answer/id #uuid "b33ae4fd-7df5-5668-be3f-6da8b92a1f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095408} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c620ec-258c-57ed-8f58-6c1af87e31f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095409} {:answer/id #uuid "30ae4bc2-f079-544b-81c3-abc3d5c10ec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095410} {:answer/id #uuid "497ee82d-da93-5f82-adc3-3cb7e1142e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b33ae4fd-7df5-5668-be3f-6da8b92a1f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095408} :answer-field/id #uuid "d50d9198-c7df-55ec-ba39-bff28ab4846e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095406}] :question/id #uuid "544be85e-c712-5922-8992-f82de75c2029" :question/math-academy-id "q-48391" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y = 2e^{x}(x + 1)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = 0$." :question/worked-solution "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\left(2 x + 2\\right) e^{x}\\right)=\\left(2 x + 2\\right) e^{x} + 2 e^{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given point gives\n\n$$\n4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097260 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c7eb625-3ff4-5e82-bd70-a085123a70c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3π^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095485} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b825b6-1cae-5e24-9e36-665ccf694b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6π^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095486} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab1f0af-b2c2-5a25-97d0-1ea8b6003204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3π^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095487} {:answer/id #uuid "5e676af8-cf84-5f73-998c-145d20246a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095488} {:answer/id #uuid "73d74933-2b73-5e41-8a53-45938d45db82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6π^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d74933-2b73-5e41-8a53-45938d45db82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6π^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095489} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2dfab29-1db5-50bf-875c-fe928ce84d34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095484}] :question/id #uuid "1feafbad-2c59-53b5-8e99-0aba4e213ff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-48901" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y = 8x^{3}\\sin x$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = \\frac{π}{2}$." :question/worked-solution "Use the product rule, $(uv)′=u′v+uv′$, and differentiate each factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(8 x^{3} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)=8 x^{3} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 24 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given point gives\n\n$$\n6 \\pi^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d88db36a-1743-57b4-81de-ba3e94f146e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d88db36a-1743-57b4-81de-ba3e94f146e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232540} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cf0faa2-183e-595b-9158-aab3d3891b84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a902a53e-f058-534a-bee4-004868eb968b" :question/math-academy-id "q-310188" :question/problem "Differentiate ${3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}(x).$\n\n$({3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}(x))^{'}=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{3}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}(x))^{'} & ={u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x) \\\\  & =({3}^{x})^{'}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}(x)+{3}^{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}(x))^{'} \\\\  & =({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3))(\\operatorname{sin}(x))+({3}^{x})(\\operatorname{cos}(x)) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)\\operatorname{sin}(x)+{3}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233776 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d79a7bd8-521e-5538-bc94-8c3a64e6621d" :question/math-academy-id "q-31226" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{tan}x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=3{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{tan}x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={sec}^{2}x.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})({sec}^{2}x)+(\\operatorname{tan}x)(6x) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{sec}^{2}x+6x\\operatorname{tan}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=\\pi } & =3{x}^{2}{sec}^{2}x+6x\\operatorname{tan}x{|}_{x=\\pi } \\\\  & =3(\\pi )^{2}{sec}^{2}(\\pi )+6(\\pi )\\operatorname{tan}(\\pi ) \\\\  & =3{\\pi }^{2}\\cdot 1+6\\pi \\cdot 0 \\\\  & =3{\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $3{\\pi }^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "131acbe9-558d-5eca-b043-6011320bbf1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{tan}(x)-2)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "131acbe9-558d-5eca-b043-6011320bbf1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{tan}(x)-2)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232577} :answer-field/id #uuid "db20f675-f846-587b-8b98-472e5b4e4ce4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "04a32680-52e9-52f1-b831-14d1889bed06" :question/math-academy-id "q-319402" :question/problem "Differentiate $(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\operatorname{cos}(x)$\n\n$((2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\operatorname{cos}(x))^{'}=-{sec}^{2}(x)\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=2-\\operatorname{tan}(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\operatorname{cos}(x))^{'} & ={u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x) \\\\  & =(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))^{'}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}(x)+(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}(x))^{'} \\\\  & =(-{sec}^{2}(x))(\\operatorname{cos}(x))+(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))(-\\operatorname{sin}(x)) \\\\  & =-{sec}^{2}(x)\\operatorname{cos}(x)+(\\operatorname{tan}(x)-2)\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e6108cd-c0ec-571c-ad0a-13dc2e7b511f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(5)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232579} {:answer/id #uuid "dec63f26-4bc5-4a1b-82e6-38b3bd6341a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670944} {:answer/id #uuid "040e6cf7-0789-41fd-a4fe-d511c15e7a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670945} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9a1076-00fc-4cab-9ade-a3329f1c19bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x\\ln" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670946} {:answer/id #uuid "32150198-ed6d-42a1-bb94-405669a0f294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x\\ln5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670947} {:answer/id #uuid "18b41c1b-22a4-48fe-a0ca-2f2261787e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x\\ln5\\sin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670948} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce6a3cf-71ad-414a-988a-bed5e2a378f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x\\ln5\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e6108cd-c0ec-571c-ad0a-13dc2e7b511f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(5)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232579} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d91600c-0002-59f3-81a1-16e9bcfd0e5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "11843f86-fdb6-56e0-8408-0d8387a30533" :question/math-academy-id "q-319421" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={5}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}(x),$ find ${f}^{'}(x).$\n\n${f}^{'}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{5}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={5}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & ={({5}^{x})}^{'}\\operatorname{sin}(x)+{5}^{x}{(\\operatorname{sin}(x))}^{'} \\\\  & =({5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(5))\\operatorname{sin}(x)+{5}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}(x)) \\\\  & ={5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(5)\\operatorname{sin}(x)+{5}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9bc784-4648-528a-ac26-6d3516a71384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b9bc784-4648-528a-ac26-6d3516a71384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232589} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2fdd90-ea5c-5dc2-bea7-c9bda09ae803" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3c831400-ba54-50fb-91a6-b9b14e55efca" :question/math-academy-id "q-319825" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(x-1)\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x-1$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(x-1)\\cdot \\frac{2}{2x+1}+\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x-1)}{2x+1}+\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{2(0-1)}{2(0)+1}+\\operatorname{ln}(2(0)+1) \\\\  & =(-2)+\\operatorname{ln}(1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb3cf46d-4dfa-538f-ba3e-cfde7c2bd873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb3cf46d-4dfa-538f-ba3e-cfde7c2bd873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232591} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac9d63dd-c99e-5f08-8d1a-09b6cb6e69fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ab210aae-e5d2-52de-b35d-cb8603b929bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-319909" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{2x},$ find ${f}^{'}(x).$\n\n${f}^{'}(x)=2x{e}^{2x}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)={e}^{2x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{'}{e}^{2x}+{x}^{2}({e}^{2x})^{'} \\\\  & =(2x)({e}^{2x})+({x}^{2})(2{e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =2x{e}^{2x}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234296 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2b5dea81-9340-51d4-993f-9f9ce501ae79" :question/math-academy-id "q-71004" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x)^{'} & ={u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{'}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}x)^{'} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(\\operatorname{sin}x)+({e}^{x})(\\operatorname{cos}x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ead734d2-e970-5e92-9ac3-1260bbfab982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ead734d2-e970-5e92-9ac3-1260bbfab982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234918} :answer-field/id #uuid "3429cda5-daf9-53dc-9c18-72e4afbade0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dabe687a-249f-595c-be70-5214c92992e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-167326" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\nSlope $\\,=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}+h\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2{e}^{\\pi }.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbf988f2-8940-5547-8a0c-461e7fba4865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbf988f2-8940-5547-8a0c-461e7fba4865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234891} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6fb57fa-80a8-5893-88ed-795c73c49674" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8af2c303-b3aa-5790-885e-7a978a609bf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-167780" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\nSlope $\\,=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}+h\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2{e}^{\\pi }.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20897b11-31f3-5236-8344-066364ab30aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238339} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9dc0f2-2211-5b4e-a2e7-26a81ec7f21c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x+\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238465} {:answer/id #uuid "528c811e-a747-5b55-b5c7-a2d707220097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238765} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cd3281-ae65-5560-8442-2a603e50ff12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x+\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239827} {:answer/id #uuid "cce47b31-03c3-57e4-ae08-02ac34ba2a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "528c811e-a747-5b55-b5c7-a2d707220097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238765} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0d6216-93d3-5d7b-aefb-cbdf2e8a0a46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d7240cf-a773-5ae8-8c7e-03955317789e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104297" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}cos⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}cos⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (cos⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(cos⁡x)+({e}^{x})(-sin⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40427a01-e865-553d-9978-a8f9a86f4287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251086} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3624d4-0726-5e76-8ec2-c6738c5615aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251193} {:answer/id #uuid "a5e9eb2f-18a3-50d7-9c4e-0a47c7a87ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251984} {:answer/id #uuid "b56383b5-a0ac-53ad-a0fe-2a36c1ab2610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252146} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1a7c18-5e33-593a-86b3-851a45507a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5e9eb2f-18a3-50d7-9c4e-0a47c7a87ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251984} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce3d68b-66a4-51fa-a4ba-3670771baf6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "11c94822-e3fa-5674-8f0a-3b72546b7b89" :question/math-academy-id "q-11841" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=x\\cdot {3}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)={3}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}\\cdot {3}^{x}+x\\cdot ({3}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & ={3}^{x}+(x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x}) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x} \\\\  & =(1+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3){3}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1371ebf8-eb22-510a-8da9-ab71603cf224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284960} {:answer/id #uuid "53d9fa80-4531-56fa-a24b-26f7f44fadfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285560} {:answer/id #uuid "7e63c504-8cfa-54d7-aead-931836c675c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2{e}^{x}+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285950} {:answer/id #uuid "8f418a4b-7d9e-52b0-a17c-229783a68355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286094} {:answer/id #uuid "904ec37a-bb54-5997-a86e-3970a5f9817d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(x{e}^{x}+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1371ebf8-eb22-510a-8da9-ab71603cf224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284960} :answer-field/id #uuid "4af7b461-8f62-58e4-ac36-73b94cae5741" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5d5b2e99-3a45-59ab-9bf2-0e86debf5990" :question/math-academy-id "q-1916" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{′}{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =(2x)({e}^{x})+({x}^{2})({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2x{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =(x+2)x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329a0351-2458-5dc2-afb3-fb83d076e70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sec}x+{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285251} {:answer/id #uuid "3d41ba8e-fd4a-5c5b-8e2c-3eb30e482c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{tan}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285366} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2ff268-76d1-583f-9abe-62b917b9c7eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{csc}^{2}x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{tan}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285621} {:answer/id #uuid "93783351-25ff-5c87-8ae9-958c98c327e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}x+\\operatorname{tan}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286129} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7d1570-7a65-5731-b765-bf52675c003d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{tan}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb7d1570-7a65-5731-b765-bf52675c003d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{tan}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286945} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44b9e2e-ea9e-5094-bc4f-bc781e7df5d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a541e9ea-7fd8-5568-9e5c-f9ef03f5eaf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-1931" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}tan⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=tan⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}tan⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot tan⁡x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (tan⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(tan⁡x)+({e}^{x})({sec}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "733a21b6-530d-58ad-a226-6cac63423ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{\\operatorname{ln}10}-\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{log}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285849} {:answer/id #uuid "b59cbc6b-900a-5727-b8b9-ede6d31b43fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x}-\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{log}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286442} {:answer/id #uuid "b7de04db-df2e-5b86-833c-791e2ab5c775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x\\operatorname{ln}10}+\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{log}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286464} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d4f500-323e-5311-9fac-df967ad59f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x\\operatorname{ln}10}-\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{log}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286604} {:answer/id #uuid "df108f3b-d4a9-5d27-b27b-ac44d2256aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x}-\\operatorname{sin}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5d4f500-323e-5311-9fac-df967ad59f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x\\operatorname{ln}10}-\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{log}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286604} :answer-field/id #uuid "87489006-c764-5370-a687-c0a258ab9b3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7d56c895-83f0-5d1c-bce1-e5e5d8df4d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-1934" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=cos⁡xlog⁡x,$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=cos⁡x$ and $v(x)=log⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(cos⁡x)}^{′}log⁡x+cos⁡x{(log⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =(-sin⁡x)(log⁡x)+(cos⁡x)\\left(\\frac{1}{xln⁡10}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{cos⁡x}{xln⁡10}-sin⁡xlog⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bac31f3f-82dd-5744-9c52-62141c569e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+\\operatorname{sin}(x)){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac31f3f-82dd-5744-9c52-62141c569e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+\\operatorname{sin}(x)){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298365} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d13588f-071e-5a52-a869-877b2c497c93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c9a55990-04ba-5f4c-bd0b-a335f0aeb15a" :question/math-academy-id "q-319350" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}(2+sin⁡(x)).$\n\n$({e}^{x}(2+sin⁡(x)))^{′}=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{e}^{x}cos⁡(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=2+sin⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}sec⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot (2+sin⁡(x))+{e}^{x}\\cdot (2+sin⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(2+sin⁡(x))+({e}^{x})(cos⁡(x)) \\\\  & =(2+sin⁡(x)){e}^{x}+{e}^{x}cos⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70915bcc-86df-54d2-a4fe-50e0b9f25633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70915bcc-86df-54d2-a4fe-50e0b9f25633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298034} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c11172-6006-5675-abeb-a1bc58910b0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dca45644-472a-517e-a9dd-987f8f5907bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-319357" :question/problem "Differentiate $2{x}^{2}cos⁡(x).$\n\n$(2{x}^{2}cos⁡(x))^{′}=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,2{x}^{2}sin⁡(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=2{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{2}cos⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡(x)+2{x}^{2}\\cdot (cos⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =(4x)(cos⁡(x))+(2{x}^{2})(-sin⁡(x)) \\\\  & =4xcos⁡(x)-2{x}^{2}sin⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "284d504d-e400-57ba-866e-f8dff66216fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "284d504d-e400-57ba-866e-f8dff66216fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297724} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecb4d22f-ab7d-5aa3-8db2-cf3a5509f8ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9df2a3ce-ad57-5588-83d2-42b69ca3314d" :question/math-academy-id "q-319385" :question/problem "Differentiate $\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x).$\n\n$(\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x))^{′}=\\frac{tan⁡(x)}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $v(x)=tan⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{x})^{′}\\cdot tan⁡(x)+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (tan⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}(tan⁡(x))+(\\sqrt{x})({sec}^{2}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{tan⁡(x)}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299759 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd6401f2-6da7-5c65-8aa1-add3b78f3859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{x}{sec}^{2}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd6401f2-6da7-5c65-8aa1-add3b78f3859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{x}{sec}^{2}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298448} :answer-field/id #uuid "26876702-3fb0-5366-a888-d8bd68fa6992" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6ccc1718-8889-5c4c-8f82-a3c2895dd7ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-319425" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={4}^{x}tan⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={4}^{x}ln⁡(4)tan⁡(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={4}^{x}$ and $v(x)=tan⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({4}^{x})}^{′}tan⁡(x)+{4}^{x}{(tan⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({4}^{x}ln⁡(4))tan⁡(x)+{4}^{x}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)) \\\\  & ={4}^{x}ln⁡(4)tan⁡(x)+{4}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94fe4615-3627-5184-b596-faacf4579fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94fe4615-3627-5184-b596-faacf4579fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298195} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5b5855-e173-5cc0-be78-e8c7ed94613e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6dd1a867-f879-56d0-b4c0-d0297b5035d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-319806" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(x+2)cos⁡x,$ then the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x+2$ and $v(x)=cos⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-sin⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(x+2)\\cdot (-sin⁡x)+cos⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-(x+2)sin⁡x+cos⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}} & =-(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2)sin⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+cos⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2)(1)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a9ff769-7920-54d9-9d56-bc88c33849af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a9ff769-7920-54d9-9d56-bc88c33849af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298084} :answer-field/id #uuid "4571a1bf-33ea-5e4c-ab47-61e0c018609f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c6b71a24-90f7-5ca7-b521-491ff5b33ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319829" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(x-1)ln⁡(4x-3),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x-1$ and $v(x)=ln⁡(4x-3).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4}{4x-3}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(x-1)\\cdot \\frac{4}{4x-3}+ln⁡(4x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=1$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & =(1-1)\\cdot \\frac{4}{4(1)-3}+ln⁡(4(1)-3) \\\\  & =0+ln⁡(1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bfce910-f1a6-55e0-aa0a-ef391e8972f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bfce910-f1a6-55e0-aa0a-ef391e8972f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298162} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b17fdea-2304-5379-9c2f-9f4ff86470d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dcf49dc9-80d7-5610-a247-cb1da3f12efe" :question/math-academy-id "q-319842" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=({x}^{2}-4x+7){e}^{x},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{2}-4x+7$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x-4,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-4x+7)\\cdot {e}^{x}+{e}^{x}\\cdot (2x-4) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({x}^{2}-2x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={{e}^{x}({x}^{2}-2x+3)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0-0+3)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308e34e3-3155-5d60-9431-e03d0af4fa0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297757} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ed3fa-86d1-4803-8dcc-ef4b061d6628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^2e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308e34e3-3155-5d60-9431-e03d0af4fa0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297757} :answer-field/id #uuid "f623b835-9c91-54d1-9180-2267f616a2e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b53a0674-b02c-54b5-9306-2aa04fbf2674" :question/math-academy-id "q-319902" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{3}{e}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{x}^{3}{e}^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{3}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{3})^{′}{e}^{x}+{x}^{3}({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})({e}^{x})+({x}^{3})({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{x}+{x}^{3}{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "401c2c7b-6e36-5f00-8952-5abb22a759f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "401c2c7b-6e36-5f00-8952-5abb22a759f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297807} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f735430-71e8-5777-be52-a2e57f486a49" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7e457c64-526b-50d2-a5e1-9c9608789ec6" :question/math-academy-id "q-319903" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=5{x}^{2}{e}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=10x{e}^{x}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=5{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(5{x}^{2})^{′}{e}^{x}+5{x}^{2}({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =(10x)({e}^{x})+(5{x}^{2})({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =10x{e}^{x}+5{x}^{2}{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2303e32-8b26-55ec-9d0f-18e1bc3899cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3){log}_{3}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2303e32-8b26-55ec-9d0f-18e1bc3899cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3){log}_{3}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298462} :answer-field/id #uuid "792dd6e3-1db8-586c-a5f7-0da2170dac92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d825ca35-2305-5442-afb6-a99517062893" :question/math-academy-id "q-320814" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}{log}_{3}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{{3}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)={log}_{3}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({3}^{x})}^{′}{log}_{3}⁡(x)+{3}^{x}{({log}_{3}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))({log}_{3}⁡(x))+({3}^{x})\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\right) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3){log}_{3}⁡(x)+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca46b1c5-ece7-5119-abe8-777dcc7ec3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{4}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca46b1c5-ece7-5119-abe8-777dcc7ec3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{4}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298433} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aa44b57-7202-5d5a-9c5f-cd88604e7d86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6161762d-7ca8-5487-95de-c569a1e07882" :question/math-academy-id "q-320815" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={4}^{x}{log}_{4}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4){log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={4}^{x}$ and $v(x)={log}_{4}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({4}^{x})}^{′}{log}_{4}⁡(x)+{4}^{x}{({log}_{4}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4))({log}_{4}⁡(x))+({4}^{x})\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\right) \\\\  & ={4}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4){log}_{4}⁡(x)+\\frac{{4}^{x}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e34c232-975f-51cf-8ed5-ecf0f78eff8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{5}^{-x}\\operatorname{ln}(5){log}_{7}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297797} {:answer/id #uuid "8a591582-6e6f-4147-9d4d-ddb81a77153c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5^{-x}\\ln5\\left(\\log_7x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e34c232-975f-51cf-8ed5-ecf0f78eff8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{5}^{-x}\\operatorname{ln}(5){log}_{7}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297797} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b389b0c-f96f-5746-b4d1-da5e3f5fb10c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "42b535b3-90b5-5bc5-bbb3-36d4082e369c" :question/math-academy-id "q-320816" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={5}^{-x}{log}_{7}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{{5}^{-x}}{xln⁡(7)}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={5}^{-x}$ and $v(x)={log}_{7}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({5}^{-x})}^{′}{log}_{7}⁡(x)+{5}^{-x}{({log}_{7}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =(-{5}^{-x}ln⁡(5))({log}_{7}⁡(x))+({5}^{-x})\\left(\\frac{1}{xln⁡(7)}\\right) \\\\  & =-{5}^{-x}ln⁡(5){log}_{7}⁡(x)+\\frac{{5}^{-x}}{xln⁡(7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329890 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d41e3a6-5106-5f1f-89a7-bdf0659fd667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327605} {:answer/id #uuid "5722ae40-633d-5817-9b2f-fd696d396624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327690} {:answer/id #uuid "7d059a2c-54e1-581a-9631-274cba73cd9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328010} {:answer/id #uuid "e54916ae-cb46-54d5-9769-ffc8af47b71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328941} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1b3eab-bf60-5779-ac14-8316a78be3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5722ae40-633d-5817-9b2f-fd696d396624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327690} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4c9edf-2978-575c-9b65-ca2b012c2b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "33d86109-fb1d-5bea-8ffd-bc18d4e7651a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48515" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(3x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=3x-2$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(3x-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3x-2}{x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=1$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{3x-2}{x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1)-2}{1}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02bc770f-35b5-51f7-ac23-0dd7e7626849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326966} {:answer/id #uuid "a57078c9-1989-5bc2-8b84-47cb7c7b7fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328362} {:answer/id #uuid "acccd38a-7649-5753-9632-b00f2c05b4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328433} {:answer/id #uuid "bce8eacc-997c-5af0-a8a5-5af0dda6e688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi {e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328578} {:answer/id #uuid "d019d383-2037-503a-8480-3e5bdb84df98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi {e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acccd38a-7649-5753-9632-b00f2c05b4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328433} :answer-field/id #uuid "8008b7a2-773f-5257-8a67-dd590b27a6d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e7dfe1e7-2a9e-5927-a9e6-a1ed58369b31" :question/math-academy-id "q-48516" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y={e}^{x}sin⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=sin⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=cos⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot cos⁡x+(sin⁡x)\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(cos⁡x+sin⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & ={{e}^{x}(cos⁡x+sin⁡x)|}_{x=\\pi } \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =-{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-{e}^{\\pi }.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122dcace-6bca-59bb-b96f-a96026e9a833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327088} {:answer/id #uuid "29771cef-6628-575d-b6d2-039fa89b2a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327286} {:answer/id #uuid "3101f4e9-df22-5461-be7e-f6674a765dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327368} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e4fd4c-0122-574c-8317-faf21984d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328648} {:answer/id #uuid "e154d586-179b-57cc-acf3-bc95bc04c67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3e4fd4c-0122-574c-8317-faf21984d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328648} :answer-field/id #uuid "745d0171-7216-5576-96bb-4a33b2c2f9b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1066779d-ebe1-53a9-ad1f-5e9c5ee1f7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48517" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=({x}^{3}-1){e}^{x},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{3}-1$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =({x}^{3}-1)\\cdot {e}^{x}+{e}^{x}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=2$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={{e}^{x}({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1)|}_{x=2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}({2}^{3}+3(2)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =19{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $19{e}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb89b95-0bba-5b10-8fe3-527b548e1601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327074} {:answer/id #uuid "8a5aa1e3-21ee-5889-8055-e0735761bea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328124} {:answer/id #uuid "c4cf7b66-0f01-5eca-acc9-cb3a3d67bb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328659} {:answer/id #uuid "d10f42e2-911f-5fb9-b0b0-c03a2475a986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328770} {:answer/id #uuid "e360ba04-1df2-5392-a2fb-baf0e0e1b838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fb89b95-0bba-5b10-8fe3-527b548e1601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327074} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7bf395d-b055-550a-8f21-50f7bb4a70c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4a6705a9-7a56-57af-9eab-fa453a263686" :question/math-academy-id "q-48993" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=e$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=e} & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡e \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2f634bf-1fab-5c5c-9faf-cca696e95edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2f634bf-1fab-5c5c-9faf-cca696e95edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514126} :answer-field/id #uuid "f49d4659-1c96-5a65-a285-84ed00e2cd31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d1eaed8d-b238-536c-b3a6-a6e7f9e94a12" :question/math-academy-id "q-166073" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\nSlope $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}+h\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2{e}^{\\pi }.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530581 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51bdb6e8-0d6a-5328-858a-42a6f9dd4e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 x^{4} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530606} {:answer/id #uuid "6efaa9a4-cab2-5eb2-acfb-4754818a6f65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x^{3} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(4 x^{4} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530615} {:answer/id #uuid "ad98276c-d5c8-5b1d-9026-a3fde7aa4a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x^{3} \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530630} {:answer/id #uuid "af65d9db-1897-5875-8eb6-1b8506282d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x^{3} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530631} {:answer/id #uuid "d47ce2ad-7753-59d6-80e3-da03ceace85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x^{3} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - \\left(4 x^{4} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6efaa9a4-cab2-5eb2-acfb-4754818a6f65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x^{3} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(4 x^{4} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530615} :answer-field/id #uuid "9256250b-c304-500e-91d2-6794e222e1f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "00f9082d-0d86-5f9e-9f49-460c209ee39d" :question/problem "Differentiate $(4 x^{4} + 1)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=4 x^{4} + 1$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((4 x^{4} + 1)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(4 x^{4} + 1)'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 x^{4} + 1)\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ & =(16 x^{3})(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 x^{4} + 1)(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1) \\\\ & =4 x^{4} \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 x^{4} + 16 x^{3} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87dbb621-b492-5ed9-9fca-744bfb854b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530619} {:answer/id #uuid "93229879-9f47-5c4c-aab8-5be46908e80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\left(4 x^{3} + 4\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530623} {:answer/id #uuid "a75e554b-f8ad-5c6e-86e8-d22ddf113264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(4 x^{3} + 4\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530626} {:answer/id #uuid "e3069c21-faeb-5767-9717-d859d3f3104d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 x^{3} + 4\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530642} {:answer/id #uuid "f8223218-07f9-52d1-8b1c-5008ed47e978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a75e554b-f8ad-5c6e-86e8-d22ddf113264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(4 x^{3} + 4\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530626} :answer-field/id #uuid "e319cf66-a95b-5175-8d89-f32277bacd56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "014ac4bb-7a72-5e35-b106-ef044de05a7a" :question/problem "Differentiate $(4 x^{3} + 4)(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=4 x^{3} + 4$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((4 x^{3} + 4)(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(4 x^{3} + 4)'\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 x^{3} + 4)\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ & =(12 x^{2})(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 x^{3} + 4)(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ & =4 x^{3} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26daf466-ef29-5d18-b4d6-0b19055ad7ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(16 x^{3} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\right) + \\left(4 x^{4} + x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530592} {:answer/id #uuid "42486479-f5a7-5637-948a-c46eceaa8bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 x^{4} + x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530599} {:answer/id #uuid "4d185028-a8dc-5cf3-b80d-54893105586a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(16 x^{3} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530603} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8e712e-998c-5923-9a65-60879d820f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(16 x^{3} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530621} {:answer/id #uuid "bd61ff04-8b40-58b9-898f-2e05d4e13a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(16 x^{3} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\right) - \\left(4 x^{4} + x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26daf466-ef29-5d18-b4d6-0b19055ad7ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(16 x^{3} + 1\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\right) + \\left(4 x^{4} + x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530592} :answer-field/id #uuid "112b676a-b69f-5e1f-83ff-392d7c57da23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "08394ee5-3a76-579f-a293-88b55155a354" :question/problem "Differentiate $(4 x^{4} + x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=4 x^{4} + x$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((4 x^{4} + x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(4 x^{4} + x)'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2)+(4 x^{4} + x)\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2)' \\\\ & =(16 x^{3} + 1)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2)+(4 x^{4} + x)(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1) \\\\ & =4 x^{4} \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 x^{4} + 16 x^{3} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 32 x^{3} + x \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + x + \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a80d4dc-bef7-5ff9-88ce-c4c268f75691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(4 - x^{2}\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530589} {:answer/id #uuid "29056302-92aa-50a1-b474-327ae7c90b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 - x^{2}\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530593} {:answer/id #uuid "40a40a5e-3688-5c60-8cac-0f9ff9dc5999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530598} {:answer/id #uuid "ac541620-4275-579e-8eae-ccf443e63610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - \\left(4 - x^{2}\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530629} {:answer/id #uuid "f54dde14-0dd0-54c2-aa03-cdb0ea9d9a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a80d4dc-bef7-5ff9-88ce-c4c268f75691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(4 - x^{2}\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530589} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b901964-9be0-5e19-8237-fc69bdaec8af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "510fd763-1a95-5bb1-8519-840cc0dd1707" :question/problem "Differentiate $(4 - x^{2})(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=4 - x^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((4 - x^{2})(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(4 - x^{2})'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 - x^{2})\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ & =(- 2 x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 - x^{2})(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1) \\\\ & =- x^{2} \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} - x^{2} - 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530609 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a858214-1b81-50a7-b52b-e61abebcbd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 - 2 x\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3\\right) - \\left(- x^{2} + 4 x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530586} {:answer/id #uuid "54718cfb-5c9a-5467-81fb-01abf2032247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 - 2 x\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530607} {:answer/id #uuid "bd624785-7d25-59cf-997c-a90ff8f0e27d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 - 2 x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530634} {:answer/id #uuid "e9065788-56d5-5b23-a785-2d6e6b0cc735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 - 2 x\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3\\right) + \\left(- x^{2} + 4 x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530645} {:answer/id #uuid "ed867b8c-ff4b-51d9-996b-6cf1bc9856f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- x^{2} + 4 x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9065788-56d5-5b23-a785-2d6e6b0cc735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 - 2 x\\right) \\left(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3\\right) + \\left(- x^{2} + 4 x\\right) \\left(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530645} :answer-field/id #uuid "375478e3-bc5f-59c3-8422-30968f2c8f94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "58b0ec5d-8f12-5457-8e04-8865bf9e217c" :question/problem "Differentiate $(- x^{2} + 4 x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=- x^{2} + 4 x$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((- x^{2} + 4 x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(- x^{2} + 4 x)'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3)+(- x^{2} + 4 x)\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3)' \\\\ & =(4 - 2 x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 3)+(- x^{2} + 4 x)(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1) \\\\ & =- x^{2} \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} - x^{2} + 4 x \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 10 x + 4 \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} - 12\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530616 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03403a80-261a-55a5-811d-86be3111f82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(12 x^{2} + 4\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530583} {:answer/id #uuid "361c3e8d-6518-5aa3-b6fb-f9ff92036099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 x^{3} + 4 x\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530594} {:answer/id #uuid "43a3772e-3d63-5146-b44e-05174cd970a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(12 x^{2} + 4\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4\\right) + \\left(4 x^{3} + 4 x\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530601} {:answer/id #uuid "b9313533-1638-5458-9f87-aa5680e5c6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(12 x^{2} + 4\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4\\right) - \\left(4 x^{3} + 4 x\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530632} {:answer/id #uuid "c8710a91-1d8d-5afc-9805-9fbdfbde5aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(12 x^{2} + 4\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43a3772e-3d63-5146-b44e-05174cd970a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(12 x^{2} + 4\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4\\right) + \\left(4 x^{3} + 4 x\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\